WEBVTT

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:24.450
Brother, it's starting.

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:25.770
Yeah.

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:27.440
Everyone, I’m counting on you.

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:30.300
You’re our final hope.

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:35.980
Is this Kusanagi’s doing?

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:39.220
We can't get to Zaizen easily.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:42.060
Bro, there are twelve opponents.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:45.690
Will we be okay?  I’m losing confidence.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:51.160
Everyone does have higher ratings than you.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:53.730
What are ratings?

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:58.580
You may not know this, but 
duelists have ratings.

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:01.240
They’re around here.

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:04.880
Playmaker is missing.

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:07.680
Playmaker is around here.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:10.500
What?  Playmaker is down there?

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:14.490
He only looked strong because I was with him.

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:15.880
Anyway...

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.180
I’m here.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:20.760
That high?

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:23.460
I’m on a different level than them.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:25.420
Impressive, Bro!

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:27.400
But you’re a problem.

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:30.260
Where am I?

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:32.810
Here.

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:34.910
What?  That low?

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:38.260
Of course.  You have no dueling history.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:40.180
Do you want to raise your rating?

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:41.380
I do!

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:44.020
Then you’re lucky.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:48.050
There are many powerful opponents 
today to gain experience points.

00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:50.360
If you work hard, you can rise quickly.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:54.590
Is that true?  I’m getting inspired!

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:56.090
I'm counting on you.

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:58.170
Let's begin the plan!

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:09.280
calling & feeling  I take your 
thoughts to heart  VRAINS

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:37.250
The data storm grazes my cheek, 
so I can't open my eyes

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:47.160
What are we trying to find?  
Where are we trying to go?

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:52.400
I won't make anyone sad anymore

00:02:52.760 --> 00:03:00.940
I'll retrieve you  Let's go and look ahead

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:06.080
By meeting you, the world is in color

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:11.750
I'll protect you with an unseen bond

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:16.060
calling  With invisible wings

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:26.670
Destroy the dark and weakness within me

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:40.230
They’re coming!

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:44.700
Playmaker, Soulburner, Revolver!  
I’m counting on you!

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:46.130
Roger!

00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:51.780
They split into three!

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:56.250
Three?  There’s someone 
other than Ai and Roboppi?

00:03:56.250 --> 00:04:00.220
Whoever it is, I'll show no mercy 
if they're helping the Ignis!

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:11.660
Ai!

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:16.650
I found Ai!

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:22.540
Hey, Playmaker.  Long time no see.

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:25.340
Ai, why did you attack humans?

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:29.010
You wanted humans and Ignis to coexist!

00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:31.160
That’s a dream that can’t come true.

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:34.490
By chasing that dream, 
I'm the only Ignis left.

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:38.260
That’s why I decided to 
carry on Lightning’s wishes.

00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:41.880
Lightning?  What are you talking about?

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:45.500
Lightning's ego made him 
into humanity’s enemy.

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:48.500
You know all about that!

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:50.970
Yeah, I do.

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:53.970
But I’ve made my decision.

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:57.940
Besides, everyone's here to defeat me.

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:02.150
You’re wrong!  You tried 
to save Flame and Aqua!

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:04.850
But I couldn’t save them.

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:07.180
We had no choice!

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:10.860
There's no difference, at least for me.

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:15.590
In the end, I must choose 
to live as an Ignis.

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:16.800
Ai...

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:20.960
What?

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:22.270
What’s going on?

00:05:22.270 --> 00:05:24.240
There are three Ais!

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:25.380
What?

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:32.130
Soulburner, you hate me, right?

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:34.120
It’s fine to hate me.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:36.250
I’m the one who erased Flame.

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:39.250
AI, I don’t hate you.

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:43.220
And I know Flame doesn't want this either!

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:49.430
But we can't know for sure 
because he’s no longer around.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:57.400
Revolver, I can’t believe you’re 
SOL Technologies’s lapdog.

00:05:57.400 --> 00:06:01.640
I knew it'd be my destiny to erase you.

00:06:01.640 --> 00:06:03.380
Maybe so.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:06.880
Because it wouldn’t be 
nice to steal your fun.

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:09.380
Which one's the real one?

00:06:09.380 --> 00:06:12.680
They need to check.

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:15.620
Playmaker, Soulburner and Revolver!

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:17.220
Yeah!

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:18.360
I know!

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:22.410
Ai, I can’t let you go any further!

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:29.070
I'll stop you!  And save you!

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:34.140
Go ahead and try, Playmaker!

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:35.440
Duel!

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:39.360
It’s started!

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:40.480
I’m counting on you!

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:43.560
I’ll go first.  My turn.

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:47.150
I activate the Field Spell, Ignister AiLand!

00:06:47.780 --> 00:06:51.500
When there are no monsters 
in my Main Monster Zone...

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:56.160
...I can Special Summon a Level 4 
or lower @Ignister from my hand.

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:59.160
Appear, Achichi @Ignister!

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:02.700
Link Summon!

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:05.840
Link 1 Linguriboh!

00:07:07.540 --> 00:07:11.200
Ignister AiLand’s effect activates!

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:14.450
Appear, Doyon @Ignister!

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:17.040
Doyon’s effect activates!

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:20.080
I add an @Ignister from 
my graveyard to my hand!

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:23.090
And I Normal Summon Achichi!

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:30.090
I set Achichi, Doyon and 
Linguriboh in the Link Markers!

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:33.620
Link Summon!

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:38.140
Link 3 Fire Phoenix @Ignister!

00:07:41.510 --> 00:07:43.360
What’s this?

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:47.250
The three Ais are doing the exact same duel!

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:48.340
What?

00:07:48.340 --> 00:07:52.740
When an effect destroys Fire Phoenix 
and sends it to the graveyard...

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:55.460
...I can destroy one of your monsters.

00:07:55.460 --> 00:08:01.990
And when it uses that effect, I can Special 
Summon it from the graveyard next turn.

00:08:01.990 --> 00:08:04.800
Time for the finishing touches!

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:09.470
From my hand, I activate 
Ai Ai Wall on Fire Phoenix!

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:14.610
What’s this?

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:21.850
For each Link Marker that the targeted Link 
Monster has, I put a counter on Ai Ai Wall.

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:25.280
Fire Phoenix has three Link Markers.

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:27.260
So it has three counters!

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:34.160
When there’s a counter on this 
card, neither player can attack.

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:36.050
But don’t worry.

00:08:36.050 --> 00:08:40.130
At the end of each of our 
turns, one counter is removed.

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:42.600
So we're locked for three turns.

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:46.140
That depends on how you battle.

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:53.580
Once per turn, if a Link Monster is summoned 
to your field, I place one counter on this card.

00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:57.050
You’re going to use my 
Link Summon against me!

00:08:57.050 --> 00:08:59.280
A lockdown deck…

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:02.650
Your goal is to stall us!

00:09:02.650 --> 00:09:05.210
Impressive, Professor Revolver!

00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:06.620
How insightful.

00:09:07.530 --> 00:09:09.590
New enemies have appeared!

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:11.830
Those are the real ones!

00:09:11.830 --> 00:09:16.830
That’s right.  We’re 
copies to act as decoys.

00:09:23.810 --> 00:09:25.810
Two down.

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:28.810
Baira and Genome have been defeated!

00:09:28.810 --> 00:09:31.820
Instantly!  He’s strong!

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:35.930
Now I'll go straight to Zaizen.

00:09:35.930 --> 00:09:37.220
I won’t let you!

00:09:37.820 --> 00:09:39.560
I’m your opponent.

00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:42.790
I won’t let you pass, even 
if it costs me my life!

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:45.530
Fine.  I’ll take you on.

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:54.470
If I don’t hurry, Bro 
will clean up everyone!

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:58.050
I have to duel and get experience points!

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:05.180
Found you!

00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:09.420
You’re Blood Shepherd and Ghost Girl!

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:11.480
You’re Roboppi.

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:13.280
Please be careful.

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:15.890
I have no duel data on him.

00:10:15.890 --> 00:10:19.500
Huh?  A mysterious duel AI?

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:23.080
Nice to meet you.  I’m Pandor.

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:25.670
An anti-Ignis AI.

00:10:25.670 --> 00:10:28.320
Please go easy on me.

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:30.240
I’m Roboppi.

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:34.380
I’m not an Ignis, but I 
want you both to fight me.

00:10:34.380 --> 00:10:37.800
You want to face us simultaneously?

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:39.730
You underestimate me.

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:43.390
Brother, let’s tag up and end this fast.

00:10:43.390 --> 00:10:45.220
We still need to deal with Ai.

00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:46.360
Fine.

00:10:46.360 --> 00:10:48.850
This is my first battle.

00:10:48.850 --> 00:10:50.960
I’m looking forward to it!

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:52.130
Duel!

00:10:58.540 --> 00:11:02.010
You can choose whether to go first or second.

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:04.710
You’re very confident.

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:07.050
And one more thing.

00:11:07.050 --> 00:11:10.210
I won’t use my Skill in this duel!

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:15.220
But you're free to use your Skills.

00:11:16.450 --> 00:11:18.460
You think you're better than us.

00:11:18.460 --> 00:11:20.120
No no.

00:11:20.120 --> 00:11:25.460
I want to have a difficult duel 
to gain experience points.

00:11:25.460 --> 00:11:30.230
I never thought a housework 
AI would underestimate me.

00:11:30.970 --> 00:11:34.220
I’ll show you where you stand!

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:44.120
Follow me, Emma!

00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:46.150
Wait up, brother!

00:11:46.150 --> 00:11:48.890
Sheesh!  He's so selfish!

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:51.020
I’ll go first.

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:54.860
I summon Duplicate Drone from my hand!

00:11:58.500 --> 00:12:01.500
From my hand, Duplicate Drone’s effect!

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:07.970
I can Special Summon Duplicate Drone 
when there's another copy on my field!

00:12:09.510 --> 00:12:13.020
Scud Drone’s effect from my hand!

00:12:13.020 --> 00:12:16.410
When there’s a Drone monster on 
the field, I can Special Summon it!

00:12:20.020 --> 00:12:22.090
Link Summon!

00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:26.960
Deploy, Link 1 Battledrone Sergeant!

00:12:29.690 --> 00:12:31.600
Another Link Summon!

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:36.920
Deploy, Link 2 Battledrone Warrant!

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:41.040
Come out!  The circuit that leads to victory!

00:12:42.410 --> 00:12:46.780
I set Sergeant and Warrant 
in the Link Markers!

00:12:49.550 --> 00:12:50.780
Link Summon.

00:12:50.780 --> 00:12:55.980
Deploy, Link 3 Battledrone General!

00:12:56.590 --> 00:13:01.560
So cool!  His ace monster already appeared!

00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:05.530
I set one card and end my turn.

00:13:05.530 --> 00:13:08.500
Warrant's effect from my graveyard!

00:13:08.500 --> 00:13:12.980
When there are no monsters in my Main 
Monster Zone at the end of the turn...

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:15.510
...I Special Summon Warrant 
from my graveyard!

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:19.940
Now bring it on!

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:21.500
I will!

00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:22.910
My turn!

00:13:23.930 --> 00:13:24.880
I draw!

00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:29.050
I summon Appliancer Socketroll!

00:13:31.090 --> 00:13:34.090
From my hand, Socketroll’s effect.

00:13:34.090 --> 00:13:38.800
When there’s another copy on my 
field, I can Special Summon it!

00:13:40.700 --> 00:13:43.800
And Socketroll’s effect activates!

00:13:44.500 --> 00:13:48.820
When a different Socketroll 
is Special Summoned...

00:13:48.820 --> 00:13:52.480
...I can Special Summon 
Socketroll from my deck!

00:13:54.950 --> 00:13:58.780
Getting three monsters 
this easily is impressive.

00:13:58.780 --> 00:14:01.690
Thank you for your praise!

00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:05.260
Appear!  The circuit that guides me!

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:10.650
The summoning conditions are two 
Level 1 Appliancer monsters!

00:14:13.460 --> 00:14:15.260
Link Summon!

00:14:15.260 --> 00:14:19.800
Appear, Link 2 Appliancer Celtopus!

00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:23.240
Another Link Summon!

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:30.490
Appear!  Link 1 Appliancer Vacculephant*!

00:14:31.950 --> 00:14:33.920
Celtopus’s effect!

00:14:33.920 --> 00:14:40.280
When it’s linked, your effects 
or attacks can't target Celtopus!

00:14:41.260 --> 00:14:44.000
Vacculephant’s effect activates!

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:50.640
When it’s co-linked, I can destroy 
one monster in your Main Monster Zone!

00:14:50.640 --> 00:14:52.940
I clean up Warrant!

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:54.540
I won’t let you!

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:58.300
I activate the Continuous 
Trap, Camouflage Drone!

00:14:58.300 --> 00:15:04.500
While it's on the field, your effects 
can't target my Drone monsters!

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:07.120
Nor can they be destroyed 
in battle or by effects!

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:11.090
I failed my cleaning.

00:15:11.090 --> 00:15:16.060
In that case, I activate the spell 
card, Appliancer Reuse from my hand!

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:21.030
I Special Summon a Level 4 or lower 
Appliancer monster from my graveyard!

00:15:21.030 --> 00:15:24.040
Resurrect, Socketroll!

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:26.740
Link Summon!

00:15:28.710 --> 00:15:33.040
Link 1 Appliancer Propelion!

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:40.820
I set one card.

00:15:40.820 --> 00:15:41.820
Battle!

00:15:41.820 --> 00:15:44.860
Vacculephant attacks Warrant!

00:15:44.860 --> 00:15:47.860
But Vacculephant has 1000 ATK.

00:15:47.860 --> 00:15:52.330
Warrant has 1200 ATK, so 
how will you get past it?

00:15:52.330 --> 00:15:54.700
Now’s the time for Celtopus’s effect!

00:15:54.700 --> 00:15:59.410
When a Appliancer that's co-linked to this card battles,

00:15:59.410 --> 00:16:04.680
it gains 1000 ATK for every co-linked monster!

00:16:04.680 --> 00:16:05.910
What?

00:16:05.910 --> 00:16:09.660
Vacculephant gains 2000 ATK!

00:16:10.380 --> 00:16:12.350
3000 ATK?

00:16:12.350 --> 00:16:14.950
I won’t let you do whatever you like!

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:18.820
I activate my Skill!  Drone Craft Force!

00:16:18.820 --> 00:16:27.160
Until the end of this turn, your monster 
loses 200 ATK for every Drone in the graveyard.

00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:32.140
And a Drone Link Monster gains that ATK!

00:16:32.140 --> 00:16:35.140
There are four Drone cards in the graveyard.

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:41.960
Vacculephant loses 800 ATK, 
and Warrant gains 800 ATK.

00:16:42.580 --> 00:16:46.880
But Vacculephant still has higher ATK!

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:55.210
Are you okay, brother?

00:16:55.210 --> 00:16:57.600
It's just a scratch.

00:16:57.600 --> 00:17:03.690
Celtopus’s effect ends, so 
Vacculephant’s ATK become 200.

00:17:04.700 --> 00:17:08.270
Next, Propelion attacks Warrant!

00:17:08.270 --> 00:17:14.280
Due to Celtopus’s effect, 
Propelion gains 2000 ATK!

00:17:22.690 --> 00:17:25.690
I dealt you big damage!

00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:28.930
Propelion’s ATK return to normal.

00:17:31.160 --> 00:17:34.130
I end my turn.

00:17:34.130 --> 00:17:38.140
Camouflage Drone is destroyed 
at the end of the turn.

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:44.780
My Skill’s effect ends, so Vacculephant 
and Warrant’s ATK return to normal.

00:17:47.340 --> 00:17:51.320
You're up next, Ghost Girl.

00:17:51.320 --> 00:17:54.320
This kid fights well.

00:17:54.320 --> 00:17:55.610
Be careful.

00:17:55.610 --> 00:17:58.490
He may look like a child, but he's not.

00:17:58.490 --> 00:18:01.160
He’s an AI created by the Dark Ignis.

00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:05.400
You’re starting to 
understand how great I am!

00:18:05.400 --> 00:18:10.130
Bro made me smart and taught me many things.

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:17.610
As a result, I reached the conclusion that 
humans are the worst creatures on Earth.

00:18:18.220 --> 00:18:24.080
Humans are bad creatures who fight 
each other and pollute the world.

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:31.320
That’s why I'll turn all humans 
into my experience points.

00:18:31.320 --> 00:18:32.790
Experience points?

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:36.180
In other words, you'll be gone.

00:18:36.180 --> 00:18:40.940
If humans are gone, I can clean 
up the Earth and raise my ranking.

00:18:40.940 --> 00:18:42.530
Kill two birds with one stone!

00:18:42.530 --> 00:18:45.080
I don’t understand.

00:18:45.080 --> 00:18:47.920
It’s impossible to understand an AI.

00:18:47.920 --> 00:18:52.570
AI with free will are nothing 
more than humanity’s enemy!

00:18:52.570 --> 00:18:54.550
I agree!

00:18:54.550 --> 00:18:57.550
Humans are my enemy.

00:18:57.550 --> 00:19:01.250
Please bring it on, Ghost Girl!

00:19:02.720 --> 00:19:04.190
Here I go!

00:19:04.190 --> 00:19:07.190
My turn!  I draw!

00:19:07.190 --> 00:19:10.660
I summon Altergeist Marionetter!

00:19:13.400 --> 00:19:15.720
Marionetter’s effect!

00:19:15.720 --> 00:19:20.370
I select an Altergeist trap 
card in my deck and set it.

00:19:20.370 --> 00:19:24.340
I select Altergeist Haunted Rock!

00:19:24.340 --> 00:19:29.320
It seems like a powerful card, 
but I know what you set.

00:19:29.320 --> 00:19:31.580
So I can deal with it!

00:19:31.580 --> 00:19:34.590
Sorry, but that may not be possible.

00:19:34.590 --> 00:19:38.360
When Marionetter sets a card, 
I can activate it this turn.

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:41.790
I activate the Continuous Trap, Haunted Rock!

00:19:43.490 --> 00:19:46.500
I send one Altergeist in 
